{
 "_comment": "Headers only (256 bytes plus 256 per signal), cut from real files. The first is the PhysioNet Sleep-EDF Expanded cassette recording SC4001E0-PSG.edf, fetched by Range request; the rest were written by pyedflib 0.1.42. Every expected value in those five was checked against pyedflib's own reader at generation time. The PhysioNet case was not: pyedflib refuses to open a file whose samples are absent, and PhysioNet truncated every attempt to download all 48 MB of it. Its header is self-checking (declared header bytes 2048 = 256 x (7 + 1), records x duration = 79500 s) and its fields were read against the Sleep-EDF documentation. Two intended differences from pyedflib: it hides the EDF+ annotations channel from its signal list, so its count is this one minus annotationSignalCount, and its start time carries the sub-second offset that lives in the annotations record, not in the header.",
